@*
    A text in which one number is a figure that changes (FR-ANI-2): what is before the number,
    the number in an element of its own that says its value, and what is after it. The script
    of the pages counts the number from its old value to its new one when the value changes,
    and a page without the script shows the new number at once. A figure that is not known has
    no number: the page then says what it says otherwise, as plain text. Nothing but the text
    and the one element is written, so a number is not parted from its unit. See docs/motion.md.
*@
@if (Of is { } figure)
{
    <text>@figure.Before</text><data class="figure" value="@figure.Value">@figure.Number</data><text>@figure.After</text>
}
else
{
    <text>@Otherwise</text>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The text with its figure, or null when the figure is not known.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public PageFigure? Of { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the page says when the figure is not known.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Otherwise { get; set; }
}
